\ ff-test: lines
\ Hex literals and string escapes.
\
\ A hex literal is a cell bit pattern: all-ones is -1. Out of range, it
\ used to be retried as a real - strtod reads hex floats - and pushed a
\ double. A malformed \x / \u / \U escape is now an error rather than a
\ silent substitute character, and it no longer consumes the character
\ after it: `"\x"` used to swallow its own closing quote.

0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF . cr
0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF . cr
0x8000000000000000 . cr
-0x8000000000000000 . cr
0x1FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
-0x8000000000000001
0x1p3
99999999999999999999 f. cr

"\x41\x42é\U0001F600" type cr
"abc\x" 1 2 3
"\x4"
"\uD800"
"\U00110000"
"unterminated \x
depth . cr
